  "number": 764,
  "title": "30005453: boundary counterexample and audited positive-equilibrium candidate",
  "body": "## Result and exact scope\n\nPreserves the complete audited candidate for problem 30005453 / OWR-12697708-006, rank 798.\n\n- Literal uniqueness among all nonnegative equilibria is false: the two alternating 2/0 arrays on Z with unit vertex rates are distinct equilibria for 0 < alpha < 1.\n- The explicitly corrected theorem gives a unique strictly positive edge equilibrium and simultaneous almost-sure coordinatewise convergence of N_e(t)/t from unit counts, for 0 <= alpha < 1 on countable undirected simple graphs of uniformly bounded degree with 0 < p_v <= P < infinity. The rate infimum may be zero.\n- The positive-integer initial-count extension uses the corrected equation (9) offset. Uniform spatial convergence, initially zero edges, fractional counts, unbounded degrees, and alpha=1 are outside the accepted scope.\n- Interpreting positive equilibrium as the primary report's intended scope is an inference; the report does not explicitly impose that restriction.\n\nThe [first full audit](https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/blob/88acf20cdd5b4fe8605dab7eb27733b7deda1c47/unsolved_math_prioritization/attempts/30005453/first_audit/AUDIT.md) gives mathematical PASS. A separate [exact-v2 acceptance](https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/blob/88acf20cdd5b4fe8605dab7eb27733b7deda1c47/unsolved_math_prioritization/attempts/30005453/v2_acceptance/ACCEPTANCE.md) gives PASS for the bounded editorial delta and a [targeted second analytic review](https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/blob/88acf20cdd5b4fe8605dab7eb27733b7deda1c47/unsolved_math_prioritization/attempts/30005453/v2_acceptance/REPORT.md). These are two independent AI reviews. External specialist and novelty review remain pending; no human peer-review, journal/editorial acceptance, proof-assistant certification, priority or novelty claim is made.\n\n## Frozen history and verification\n\nThe four safe ZIPs and all 52 extracted member byte strings are unchanged. Historical PROPOSED/PENDING/no-remote-write labels remain in the freezes; the later hash-bound acceptance governs the current review outcome.\n\nAccepted v2 ZIP SHA-256: `689cd325db19a449e373441c0c7cb0ede0e103456ec857215a207b7af83d3d8d`.\nAccepted proof SHA-256: `4ab6831e31f2c55969d17089a2cefacdd3d173a54f4b00e8244a5f8a635616f4`.\n\nPublication checks passed:\n- Exact 63-file recursive packet inventory, four ZIP CRC/structure/member checks, all four manifests, and all archive/extracted-byte identities.\n- Six approved editorial substitutions in four content files plus manifest regeneration; analytic Sections 2\u20138 remain exactly 12,593 unchanged bytes.\n- Normal, optimized and relocated replay; result bytes equal the frozen originals.\n- Eleven independent delta negative controls and eight publication-integrity controls.\n- Complete remote-byte readback and replay of the actual pushed commit, including all four ZIPs and the full queue. All 64 changed files match the staged SHA-256, byte count and Git blob identity.\n\nFinite checks support arithmetic and integrity. The proof and analytic reviews supply the basis for the infinite-graph mathematical conclusion.\n\n## Queue and publication boundary\n\nOnly this row's Status, Turns and Findings change: **claimed_solved, 4/5**, recording both the literal counterexample and the corrected audited theorem. Every other queue byte, including its existing stale header, is preserved.\n\nFresh main and exact-ID/code/topic PR, branch, commit and related-target checks found no existing attempt on this target. Critical alpha=1 problem 30005454 (PR #222) and supercritical lattice problem 30005457 have distinct scopes.\n\nThe payload contains authored proof/code/audits/results, the four intact safe archives, and public verification metadata. Source PDFs, extracts, images, raw corpora and private coordination files are excluded.\n\n[Start with the packet README](https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/blob/88acf20cdd5b4fe8605dab7eb27733b7deda1c47/unsolved_math_prioritization/attempts/30005453/README.md). Draft review only; no merge, release, DOI creation or outside contact.\n",
